# VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client). `npm run dev` first.
# Run "login", then the other requests reuse its tokens.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{base}}/api/v1
# Seeded branch ids (fitmanager-infra/db/seeds/demo/001_branches_and_staff.sql). Rules come from the assignment at X-Branch-Id (D-034).
@hq = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@gulshan = 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002

### Health (outside /api)
GET {{base}}/health/ready

### @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "owner", "password": "Owner@123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.data.access_token}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.data.refresh_token}}

### Who am I: global rules + one assignment per branch, each with its rules
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rotate the refresh token (the old one stops working)
POST {{api}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}" }

### Lookups
GET {{api}}/ddl?ddl_key=branch
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sign out of this session
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refresh_token": "{{refresh}}" }

### Public site groups (D-040): each group's landing section and page switches
GET {{api}}/public/site-groups

### Blog off the home page, its page kept (a required group answers 409)
PATCH {{api}}/hq/site-groups/blog
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "section": false, "page": true }

### HQ settings (D-037, D-057, D-063): VAT rate, BIN, VAT-inclusive prices, freeze range
GET {{api}}/hq/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}

### Prices include VAT; only the fields sent change (the rate is kept to basis points)
PATCH {{api}}/hq/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vat_rate": 0.15, "vat_bin": "000123456-0101", "vat_inclusive": true, "freeze_min_days": 7, "freeze_max_days": 60 }

### Public branches and price list
GET {{api}}/public/branches

###
GET {{api}}/public/plans?branch=gulshan

### What the desk sells at Gulshan
GET {{api}}/plans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### HQ: a branch profile (only the fields sent change)
PATCH {{api}}/hq/branches/{{gulshan}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "capacity": 120, "hours": [{ "days": [6, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "open": "07:00", "close": "23:00" }, { "days": [5], "open": "16:00", "close": "21:00" }] }

### HQ: plan templates, every branch's plans, promo codes
GET {{api}}/hq/plan-templates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}

###
GET {{api}}/hq/plans?branch_oid={{gulshan}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}

### A promo code: one effect (percent, amount or waive_admission)
POST {{api}}/hq/promos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "EID25", "label": "Eid offer", "percent": 25, "valid_from": "2026-12-01", "valid_to": "2026-12-15" }

### Staff at HQ (D-055): rows with assignments and `manageable`, plus the roles you may hand out
GET {{api}}/hq/staff?status=Active
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.access_token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}

### Add a trainer with a temporary password (they must change it at sign-in, D-054)
POST {{api}}/hq/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.access_token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "trainer.new", "name": "New Trainer", "password": "Temp1234", "assignments": [{ "branch_oid": "{{gulshan}}", "role": "TRAINER" }] }

### My sessions (`current` is this one)
GET {{api}}/auth/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.access_token}}

### Phase 2: a member at Gulshan (phone as 017…, stored as +880…)
# @name member
POST {{api}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Rahim Uddin", "phone": "01712345678", "gender": "Male", "health_flags": [], "health_declared": true }

###
@member = {{member.response.body.data.oid}}
@code = {{member.response.body.data.code}}

### The plans Gulshan sells
# @name plans
GET {{api}}/plans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### Quote, then sell with a part payment (the rest becomes dues)
POST {{api}}/subscriptions/quote
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "member_oid": "{{member}}", "plan_oid": "{{plans.response.body.data[0].oid}}", "charge_admission": true }

###
# @name sale
POST {{api}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "member_oid": "{{member}}", "plan_oid": "{{plans.response.body.data[0].oid}}", "charge_admission": true, "payment": { "method": "bkash", "amount": 2000, "reference": "TX-1" } }

### Pay the dues
POST {{api}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "invoice_oid": "{{sale.response.body.data.invoice.oid}}", "method": "cash", "amount": 500 }

### Scan at the door: the decision, then the check-in
POST {{api}}/attendance/evaluate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{code}}" }

###
POST {{api}}/attendance/check-in
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "{{code}}" }

### Today at the desk, and the dashboard
GET {{api}}/cash-closing/today
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

###
GET {{api}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### The exit check (HQ): does the money reconcile over the pilot's two weeks?
GET {{api}}/hq/reconciliation?from=2026-11-06&to=2026-11-19
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{hq}}

### Portal access for the member (temporary password; the username is the member code)
POST {{api}}/members/{{member}}/portal-access
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "password": "Welcome123" }

### Phase 3: this week's timetable at Gulshan (sessions are made from the weekly rules when read)
GET {{api}}/classes/schedule
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### Book the member into a class (set @session from the timetable; a full class puts them on the waitlist)
@session = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{api}}/classes/sessions/{{session}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "member_oid": "{{member}}" }

### Trainers here, then one trainer's free PT hours on a day
GET {{api}}/trainers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

###
@trainer = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{api}}/pt/slots?trainer_oid={{trainer}}&date=2026-11-22
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### Lockers with their rentals, and the maintenance blocks
GET {{api}}/lockers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

###
GET {{api}}/maintenance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### The public timetable and trainers
GET {{api}}/public/classes?branch=gulshan

###
GET {{api}}/public/trainers?branch=gulshan

### Phase 4: the exercise library at Gulshan (HQ's and the branch's own)
GET {{api}}/exercises?muscle=quads
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

### Routine templates, then assign one to the member (a copy of its own)
GET {{api}}/routines
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

###
@template = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{api}}/members/{{member}}/routine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "template_oid": "{{template}}" }

### Records, charts and workouts a week, then the measurements
GET {{api}}/members/{{member}}/progress
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}

###
GET {{api}}/members/{{member}}/measurements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Branch-Id: {{gulshan}}
